# Firmware policy tests

Last updated: 2026-10-04 14:20 IST (UTC+05:30).

Run from the repository root:

```powershell
py -m platformio test --project-dir hardware -e native
```

The native Unity suites execute production header policies:

The selected #246 changes have seven suites and 67 native cases. Use the
actual runner output at the tested commit to confirm the count.

| Suite | Coverage |
|---|---|
| `test_telemetry_policy` | GNSS clock/quality, motion hysteresis, jumps/reacquisition, one-second moving/stopped cadence, bounded queue/retry and configuration policy |
| `test_checkpoint_journal` | Commit ordering, corruption/partial-write recovery, identity binding and bounded flash-checkpoint restoration |
| `test_firmware_update_policy` | Signed-release sequence, candidate acceptance and rollback policy |
| `test_http_response` | Bounded response parsing and status/header validation |
| `test_http_reuse_guard` | Safe persistent HTTPS reuse across response outcomes |
| `test_reset_stats` | Reset-history normalization and counters |
| `test_json_payload` | Actual ArduinoJson allocation exhaustion, schema completeness and output-capacity rejection |

Use actual runner output for case counts. Host policy tests and firmware builds
do not establish physical radio, UART, GNSS, power, TLS or fleet security
acceptance. Follow [test strategy](../../docs/testing/TEST_STRATEGY.md) and
[hardware setup](../README.md) for board-specific tests and build selection.
